course: dictionary
lesson: 7316
title: Calm and still: placid
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Placid means calm and peaceful, and not easily upset or excited. In «Toad sat straight down in the middle of the dusty road ... his face wore a placid satisfied expression», Toad is not rushing about or worrying. He is sitting still and looking pleased, so placid must mean calm.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Toad sits down, looks satisfied and murmurs "Poop-poop!" happily. Nothing in the sentence shows anger or fear, so the calm meaning fits. Try it: «his face wore a calm satisfied expression» still makes sense.
explain: Placid can also describe water. A placid lake is still and smooth, with no waves or splashes. So «a placid lake» means a lake that is calm and flat, like a mirror.
fact: Placid means calm, peaceful and not easily upset or excited.
fact: «A placid horse» means a horse that stays calm and does not get startled easily.
fact: Used about water, placid means still and smooth, as in «a placid lake».
fact: Placid is an adjective. It can change to more placid and most placid.
fact: Context clues, like sitting still or looking satisfied, help you spot a word's meaning.
exercise: «a placid horse» means what? | Loud and noisy | *Calm and not easily upset | Very hungry | Fast and wild
exercise: «The lake was placid, so smooth that the sky showed in it.» What does placid describe? | Sandy beach | Stormy waves | *Still and smooth water | A fast river
exercise: Ella says her puppy is placid. What does she mean? | It is very large | It is wild and jumps at everyone | *It stays calm and rarely gets upset | It can swim
test: «The placid cows grazed in the field, unbothered by the noisy tractor.» What does placid mean? | Covered in mud | *Calm and not easily upset | Wild and noisy | Very fast
test: «The placid pond reflected the trees.» Here placid means: | *Still and smooth | Cold and icy | Splashing and rough | Dark and muddy
exam: «Toad's placid face showed he was not worried at all.» What is the best meaning of placid? | *Calm and peaceful | Sleepy and tired | Angry and upset | Surprised
